-- title:
--   Flatness and normal components of the H₁ moduli ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and naturals $\ell_g, M'$ with $\ell_g$ prime, $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, $M' \neq 0$, $q \nmid M'$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, with finite residue field, in which the images of $\ell_g$ and $M'$ are units. Three compatibility hypotheses are assumed for all $A$-algebras $T$: that a $\Gamma_1$-point datum $(x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ of $W$ (satisfying the affine equation at $(x_P,y_P)$, $(\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell_g})(x_P)=0$, $x_Q=x_P$, $y_Q=y_P$) transports along a variable change $C$ to one of $C \bullet W$; that the $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-condition `IsGamma0PowAt` on a monic-normalised kernel factor $h$ is preserved by `kernelVariableChangeDeg`; and that divisibility of `inLineMulPoly W ℓg n x` is preserved likewise. Further data: group laws $\mathcal{G}$ on the projective models, chord–tangent and origin-normalised; a level transport $\mathcal{T}$ of raw Drinfeld pairs at $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport`; and the existence, for all $T$, of graded ring homomorphisms realising variable changes (`IsVariableChangeHom`) and coefficient maps (`IsCoefficientHom`) on the graded coordinate rings of the projective models, each pulling back the irrelevant ideal. Finally, let $P_0$ be a package representing the moduli datum of `rigidDataH1Pow A ℓg M' q …` — variable-change classes of elliptic Weierstrass curves with a $\Gamma_0(M')$-kernel family, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point, a Drinfeld $q$-basis, and the linking divisibility `IsGamma1Link` — with fine moduli ring $B_0 = P_0.B_0$ of finite type over $A$. Then $B_0$ is flat as an $A$-module, and for every minimal prime $\mathfrak{P}$ of $(\bot)$ in $B_0$ the quotient $B_0/\mathfrak{P}$ is integrally closed.
--
--   This is the Katz–Mazur style regularity statement for the moduli ring carrying full Drinfeld $q$-level together with $\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ structure: the fine moduli ring is flat over the discrete valuation base and each of its irreducible components is normal. It feeds the construction of roots of unity in the components and the flatness statement for the same package used further along the $\Gamma_1$-normality chain.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_Diamond_flat_and_isIntegrallyClosed_quotient_of_mem_minimalPrimes_levelModuliPackageAbs_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_natCast_rigidDataH1Pow.lean

